 ## Codebase Patterns
+- OpenAPI update procedure documentation follows the static-release-gate
+  pattern: keep `docs/development/openapi-update-procedure.md`, SECURITY.md,
+  CI, `scripts/verify.sh`, `internal/release/AGENTS.md`, and
+  `internal/release/openapi_update_procedure_static_test.go` in lockstep;
+  document `internal/controlplane/openapi`,
+  `internal/controlplane/httpapi/routes.go`, `openapi.Endpoint`,
+  `x-required-action`, `validate.DecodeJSON`, typed `apierr` failures,
+  `apienvelope` rendering, exact OpenAPI/handler/full-suite verification
+  commands, expected outputs, stable JSON envelopes, tenant isolation,
+  idempotency, audit, quota, isolated Postgres tests, opt-in live Dokploy
+  smoke, and redaction.
 - Fake Dokploy usage documentation follows the static-release-gate pattern:
   keep `docs/development/fake-dokploy-usage.md`, SECURITY.md, CI,
   `scripts/verify.sh`, `internal/release/AGENTS.md`, and
@@ -444,6 +455,49 @@
   - Static release tests should pin the script, binary flag, runbook, SECURITY.md gate row, CI step, and `scripts/verify.sh` together to prevent operations artifact drift.
   - Dry-run plans should show command shape and `YALLA_*` variable names only; runtime seed values stay in the env file and are never echoed.
 ---
